            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0407" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/4438: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-27T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 27,
                                1927—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>6. Legation’s telegram number 11, dated January 19, 8 a.m.<anchor n="29"
                        xml:id="d268-f1"/> It is not the intention of the Department to urge
                    President Diaz to accept any foreign government’s mediation to settle the
                    differences between the Nicaraguan Government and the revolutionary forces based
                    on the withdrawal of both President Diaz and Sacasa. You should make no more
                    efforts to encourage the Government of Guatemala to offer its good offices in
                    connection with this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
